.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-harvest-scan 1  "scan " 
.SH NAME
git\-harvest\-scan \- Harvest this branch\*(Aqs structured commits into a fragment
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-harvest scan\fR [\fB\-b\fR|\fB\-\-base\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-changelog\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Harvest this branch\*(Aqs structured commits into a fragment.
.PP
Walks the commits on the current branch back to its merge base with `\-\-base`, splits every commit subject on the CHANGELOG\*(Aqs configured delimiter into a bucket and an entry, and writes the harvested entries as one fragment file.  A commit with no delimiter, an unrecognised bucket, or the standing `Skip ::=` marker is dropped silently; a branch with nothing to harvest writes no file and exits successfully.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-base\fR \fI<BASE>\fR [default: main]
The ref the branch diverged from; its merge base bounds the walk
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-changelog\fR \fI<CHANGELOG>\fR [default: CHANGELOG.ron]
The CHANGELOG to read the harvest configuration from, if it exists
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite the fragment when one of the same name exists already
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: changelog.d]
The directory to write the fragment into
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
